From 9377cf303b82382ca651147a4d523567d36fa243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marie-222 <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:52:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] rdp: offer standard RDP security without encryption on
 a local connection (FreeRDP 3)

Without TLS and without --rdp4-key the backend sets ENCRYPTION_LEVEL_NONE, which is what a client connecting
over an external listener fd (vsock, WSLg) negotiates. FreeRDP 3 only offers standard RDP security when the
server certificate is RSA 2048 and otherwise switches it off, so the negotiation failed with 'server supports
only NLA Security'. Give it a built-in throw-away RSA 2048 key and certificate; nothing is encrypted with them.
---
 libweston/backend-rdp/rdp-local-cert.h | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libweston/backend-rdp/rdp.c            | 16 +++++++
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libweston/backend-rdp/rdp-local-cert.h

diff --git a/libweston/backend-rdp/rdp-local-cert.h b/libweston/backend-rdp/rdp-local-cert.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..cb997b2a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libweston/backend-rdp/rdp-local-cert.h
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+/*
+ * A throw-away RSA 2048 key and self-signed certificate.
+ *
+ * FreeRDP 3 only offers "standard RDP security" when the server certificate is RSA 2048 (see
+ * freerdp_peer_initialize()). WSLg's Windows client connects over vsock and asks for exactly that, with
+ * ENCRYPTION_LEVEL_NONE: nothing is encrypted with this key and it protects nothing. It is only used when
+ * neither TLS (--rdp-tls-cert/--rdp-tls-key) nor --rdp4-key is configured, i.e. for a local connection.
+ */
